Key is also restructuring Georgia Tech’s offensive staff. In addition to adjustments to on-field and in-game coaching responsibilities, the structure of Tech’s game-planning and other off-the-field duties are being revamped for the final three games of the season to address deficiencies on the offensive side of the ball. [...] defensive backs coach Vinnie Sunseri taking over defensive play-calling duties;
 assistant wide receivers coach DeAndre Hopkins serving as the primary wide receivers coach;
 assistant offensive line coach Brandon Torrey serving as the primary offensive line coach;
 assistant head coach/defensive line coach Jess Simpson coaching defensive ends and outside linebackers (in addition to defensive tackles);
 senior defensive analyst Jack Tyler coaching linebackers. [...] THE FLATS – Four Georgia Tech football coaches – defensive coordinator/linebackers coach Jason Semore, offensive line coach Allen Mogridge, outside linebackers/defensive ends coach Kyle Pope and wide receivers coach Jafar Williams – have been relieved of their duties, effective immediately, head coach Brent Key announced on Monday.
